WEBVTT

00:30.239 --> 00:31.114
Tears?

00:39.414 --> 00:41.833
Hey, what the hell happened here?

00:42.167 --> 00:43.043
Where's Inoue?!

00:44.211 --> 00:48.006
Inoue...
sacrificed her soul...

00:48.632 --> 00:50.634
to put an end to Yhwach.

00:55.847 --> 00:56.807
Are you all right?

00:57.182 --> 00:58.100
Yeah...

01:01.019 --> 01:03.647
Inoue used everything she had...

01:04.398 --> 01:06.525
to keep us together.

01:08.235 --> 01:09.361
Ichigo...

01:09.945 --> 01:12.739
This means
the world was saved, right?

01:15.492 --> 01:16.368
Not yet.

01:16.618 --> 01:17.578
Huh?

01:44.730 --> 01:46.523
Ichigo, what are you...

01:47.482 --> 01:49.359
planning to do?

01:50.986 --> 01:51.945
Ichigo!

01:52.988 --> 01:54.865
Is it that damned priest?

01:58.577 --> 01:59.453
Ichigo!

02:02.122 --> 02:03.206
You fool!

02:14.843 --> 02:15.761
Why?

02:17.763 --> 02:21.016
Why do you turn your back to me?

02:42.704 --> 02:44.081
Inoue...

02:51.213 --> 02:52.130
It's morning.

02:53.215 --> 02:54.383
Haschwalth!

02:55.092 --> 02:57.594
The time limit has already passed.

03:11.274 --> 03:13.652
The Almighty.

03:20.617 --> 03:22.744
Yhwach...

03:23.328 --> 03:25.914
Why are you here?
You're...

03:26.039 --> 03:28.083
What are you talking about?

03:29.543 --> 03:33.171
That version of the future
never existed.

03:36.133 --> 03:40.011
THE CALAMITY

03:41.930 --> 03:44.433
<i>I've lived my way full of shame</i>

03:44.516 --> 03:48.854
<i>"Envy" comes from the ways
of the eventual end</i>

03:48.895 --> 03:51.356
<i>The ambiguous balance</i>

03:51.440 --> 03:54.276
<i>I want to cut ties at once</i>

03:55.569 --> 03:57.111
<i>It's too late to back down now</i>

03:57.112 --> 03:58.362
<i>Before this senile body dies</i>

03:58.363 --> 04:00.073
<i>My shadow will fade away soon, but</i>

04:00.115 --> 04:02.284
<i>Even if I disappear, my journey won't stop</i>

04:02.325 --> 04:03.826
<i>Uncertain days, certain endings</i>

04:03.827 --> 04:05.494
<i>My stories fill the in-betweens</i>

04:05.495 --> 04:08.247
<i>Beyond the wall blocking my way,
there is a calm morning</i>

04:08.248 --> 04:12.544
<i>Like the rising sun,
I stand with the wind at my back</i>

04:12.669 --> 04:16.714
<i>A burst of hope?</i>

04:16.715 --> 04:18.967
<i>Break through an endless night</i>

04:19.009 --> 04:23.930
<i>Show the sun waiting
at the end of darkness</i>

04:24.014 --> 04:27.057
<i>The promise is yet to be fulfilled</i>

04:27.058 --> 04:30.604
<i>but I stand in solitude not to let it go</i>

04:30.645 --> 04:33.522
<i>At the moment,
I'm connecting numerous lights</i>

04:33.523 --> 04:37.235
<i>to form a constellation
that paves tomorrow</i>

04:37.903 --> 04:41.740
<i>Even if the rain clouds
hide the night sky away</i>

04:41.782 --> 04:45.243
<i>there certainly is a flame in my heart</i>

04:45.577 --> 04:50.415
<i>God is no longer reliable</i>

04:50.582 --> 04:55.295
<i>I glance up towards the silver lining</i>

04:55.420 --> 05:01.592
<i>The destiny of bursting fate</i>

05:01.593 --> 05:03.970
BLEACH THOUSAND-YEAR BLOOD WAR

05:17.943 --> 05:19.861
It's understandable that
you failed to notice,

05:19.903 --> 05:22.364
in the depths of Wahr Welt,
where the light cannot reach.

05:23.490 --> 05:26.201
Moments before you activated
Leiden Hant,

05:26.952 --> 05:29.287
His Majesty's power and mine
were swapped.

05:30.288 --> 05:36.294
My original power is more suited
for battle than His Majesty's.

05:37.337 --> 05:41.550
Especially for an enemy like you,
whose errors need rectifying!

05:43.426 --> 05:45.053
The balance has shifted.

05:46.680 --> 05:48.181
I'll let you in on something good...

05:49.516 --> 05:54.479
The true terror of The Almighty
is not the power to see the future.

05:54.938 --> 05:55.981
What does that—?

05:56.356 --> 05:58.400
I'll tell you
when our fight is over.

05:59.860 --> 06:00.735
Now...

06:01.069 --> 06:03.905
Put all that you are onto
the balance, Uryu Ishida!

06:04.489 --> 06:08.743
On your broken balance that points
to the path of no return!

06:14.207 --> 06:15.125
Guys!

06:22.424 --> 06:25.844
Did you think you are the only one
who can wield dual swords?

06:26.511 --> 06:30.473
You're looking for a hole
in my ability, aren't you?

06:33.310 --> 06:34.311
Ichigo...

06:34.936 --> 06:37.230
You have the wrong idea.

06:37.856 --> 06:42.110
The future does not lie
on a single path.

06:43.069 --> 06:46.615
The future is like
the infinite grains of sand

06:46.656 --> 06:49.242
scattered before me.

06:50.327 --> 06:56.207
Each of those seemingly isolated
and scattered grains of sand

06:56.833 --> 06:57.959
is the future.

06:59.002 --> 07:02.547
Put another way, they can
also be called possibilities.

07:03.465 --> 07:04.507
Ichigo...

07:04.758 --> 07:08.219
I enjoy speaking of hope.

07:09.387 --> 07:12.849
The future can be changed.
That is a fact.

07:13.099 --> 07:16.144
A wonderful fact filled
with such great hope.

07:16.895 --> 07:19.189
But changing the future
simply means

07:19.397 --> 07:24.653
jumping from one grain
of sand to another.

07:24.944 --> 07:30.283
And I can see every grain of sand
from high above,

07:30.325 --> 07:31.993
and intervene.

07:33.328 --> 07:37.874
The Almighty is not
the power to see the future.

07:38.291 --> 07:40.919
It is the power
to alter the future!

07:45.215 --> 07:46.049
Inoue!

07:49.886 --> 07:52.222
I'm... sorry...

07:53.932 --> 07:54.974
Ichigo...

07:55.392 --> 07:57.644
She could not protect you...

07:58.061 --> 08:00.355
That is that woman's future.

08:01.523 --> 08:04.317
You see, I altered her future.

08:05.068 --> 08:08.029
Please do not give up hope, Ichigo.

08:08.446 --> 08:11.366
Continue blindly jumping from

08:11.449 --> 08:16.121
the rolling grains of sand
called fate or possibility

08:16.204 --> 08:18.623
as you always have until now.

08:19.290 --> 08:22.961
That is hope for humans.

08:23.420 --> 08:26.756
All of us walk on a balance.

08:27.716 --> 08:32.178
We sort what is right or wrong
for ourselves.

08:33.012 --> 08:34.764
The sorted pieces
of right and wrong

08:34.889 --> 08:37.642
pile on top of each other
and give us form.

08:39.102 --> 08:40.895
That is who we are.

08:42.647 --> 08:45.942
I know you too
have done the same, Uryu Ishida.

08:47.402 --> 08:49.738
But I do not see your form.

08:50.613 --> 08:54.284
I do not see the form
you've shaped for yourself

08:54.701 --> 08:56.494
with the choices that you've made.

08:57.704 --> 09:00.290
Who are you, Uryu Ishida?

09:02.584 --> 09:07.297
Is it truly your desire
to risk your life

09:07.714 --> 09:09.674
for those shallow humans?

09:10.216 --> 09:11.926
You really talk too much.

09:13.178 --> 09:16.723
"Who am I," you ask?

09:18.016 --> 09:21.561
How the hell am I supposed
to answer that?

09:28.359 --> 09:30.111
That's something...

09:30.695 --> 09:34.199
I'll finally find out when
I defeat you people!

09:35.450 --> 09:36.326
I see.

09:46.336 --> 09:48.295
ANOMALY DETECTED
Boundary depth is increasing!

09:48.296 --> 09:48.462
ANOMALY DETECTED

09:48.463 --> 09:49.422
ANOMALY DETECTED
It's not stopping!

09:50.799 --> 09:52.509
What are the Quincies
trying to do?

09:52.842 --> 09:54.052
The world will be destroyed!

09:54.636 --> 09:58.389
I tried hitting it with Reishi
via the Garganta,

09:58.515 --> 10:01.392
but it only decreases for a moment
before reverting back!

10:01.810 --> 10:03.978
So it decreased momentarily?

10:04.312 --> 10:05.939
It did, but don't
get your hopes up.

10:06.189 --> 10:09.067
Mutual annihilation is
the only effective way.

10:09.567 --> 10:11.277
Do you mean we have no choice

10:11.402 --> 10:13.530
but to hit it with
an equal amount of energy?

10:13.696 --> 10:15.907
Where do we find that
kind of energy?

10:16.032 --> 10:18.326
We wouldn't have a problem
if we knew!

10:19.619 --> 10:21.454
We've tried everything we can.

10:21.788 --> 10:23.081
What do we do, Akon?

10:23.748 --> 10:27.127
This distortion is spreading
because the balance of souls

10:27.252 --> 10:30.088
in the World of the Living
and Soul Society is destroyed.

10:30.672 --> 10:33.174
Huh?! What are you even talking
about at this point?!

10:34.509 --> 10:36.928
What if we create balance here?

10:37.262 --> 10:38.304
Huh?!

10:42.016 --> 10:43.810
We open the gate to Hueco Mundo.

10:45.186 --> 10:47.522
Let me ask a question.

10:48.398 --> 10:52.110
Why are you asking me
what sort of person I am?

10:52.902 --> 10:54.821
Before even asking such a question,

10:55.280 --> 10:57.490
shouldn't you defeat me
as fast as you can

10:57.740 --> 11:00.493
and race back to Yhwach's side?

11:01.536 --> 11:02.787
They will die.

11:03.788 --> 11:06.291
No matter how much I toy
with you here,

11:06.916 --> 11:09.669
His Majesty will not be exposed
to any danger.

11:25.685 --> 11:28.229
You are a lucky man, Uryu Ishida.

11:28.897 --> 11:31.900
You succeeded in placing
Leiden Hant on me

11:32.233 --> 11:35.236
and shot me full of Heilig Pfeil.

11:35.820 --> 11:40.033
An equivalent amount of misfortune
will rain down on you.

11:42.911 --> 11:44.662
My Schrift is B.

11:45.705 --> 11:47.165
The Balance.

11:47.790 --> 11:50.251
By allocating the misfortunes
that occur in my domain

11:50.293 --> 11:51.794
to the fortunate,

11:52.128 --> 11:54.130
I maintain harmony in the world.

11:54.881 --> 11:57.592
You do not stand a chance,
Uryu Ishida.

11:58.343 --> 12:01.095
There are probably no more answers
I can get from you.

12:02.013 --> 12:04.098
If you have nothing to say,
then so be it.

12:04.641 --> 12:05.558
This is where it ends.

12:05.975 --> 12:06.851
Wait...

12:07.352 --> 12:09.437
Don't you want to see it?

12:10.230 --> 12:12.607
My Schrift?

12:13.358 --> 12:15.276
Don't bother trying to prolong
the inevitable.

12:15.652 --> 12:18.446
If it was enough to beat me,
you would've used it already.

12:19.572 --> 12:20.657
It's quite the opposite.

12:21.741 --> 12:23.701
I was just thinking
now's the time to use it.

12:24.786 --> 12:25.954
What do you mean?

12:26.621 --> 12:28.206
My Schrift is...

12:28.957 --> 12:29.832
A.

12:30.083 --> 12:31.334
Antithesis.

12:33.836 --> 12:35.171
Antithesis...

12:35.713 --> 12:39.008
It reverses events that
have already taken place

12:39.133 --> 12:41.052
between two designated points.

12:41.886 --> 12:43.471
This time I kept it simple—

12:43.596 --> 12:46.224
I revered our wounds.

12:47.392 --> 12:48.476
I see...

12:52.563 --> 12:55.358
What a magnificent power!

12:56.901 --> 12:59.654
No wonder His Majesty took
an interest in you.

13:00.613 --> 13:03.116
With the power to reverse events
that already taken place,

13:03.491 --> 13:05.660
perhaps you are the only one

13:06.119 --> 13:08.246
who can challenge
His Majesty's power.

13:08.997 --> 13:10.373
What does that mean?

13:10.915 --> 13:14.877
Are you talking about
the true power of The Almighty?

13:15.378 --> 13:17.505
Interpret it any way you wish.

13:18.089 --> 13:19.757
All I can say is...

13:20.049 --> 13:24.137
I was correct in stopping you here.

13:25.888 --> 13:27.807
Do you think I would let you go?!

13:29.350 --> 13:32.020
Your Antithesis is remarkable,

13:32.270 --> 13:34.689
but it does not match up well
with The Balance.

13:36.274 --> 13:39.402
I told you,
I can allocate misfortunes

13:40.111 --> 13:43.239
and all misfortunes
that occur to me

13:43.489 --> 13:46.367
are received with
this Freund Schild.

13:47.201 --> 13:48.786
In other words...

13:49.287 --> 13:52.165
The good fortune of
you wounding me

13:52.290 --> 13:55.001
has rained down on you as
misfortune in the same amount.

13:55.585 --> 13:57.920
The misfortune you inflicted
on my body

13:58.379 --> 14:00.506
is transferred to and absorbed
by Freund Schild...

14:01.799 --> 14:04.635
and will rain down on you
as additional misfortune.

14:06.387 --> 14:09.932
As I said before, you don't stand
a chance, Uryu Ishida.

14:15.646 --> 14:17.440
Still won't give up, will you?

14:18.441 --> 14:20.193
You're a smart man...

14:21.027 --> 14:23.237
I know you realize
you don't stand a chance

14:23.362 --> 14:24.989
against me or His Majesty.

14:26.991 --> 14:29.410
I said I couldn't see you...

14:29.786 --> 14:30.828
but I take that back.

14:31.454 --> 14:35.166
You are very much like...

14:35.958 --> 14:37.335
those unbelievably foolish humans.

14:39.128 --> 14:41.297
You don't understand.

14:41.756 --> 14:47.386
The Wahr Welt I desire is also
the world which that woman desires.

14:49.180 --> 14:51.474
A serene world without conflict,

14:51.599 --> 14:55.353
without pain and without
hatred or sadness.

14:56.229 --> 15:00.233
That is exactly the Wahr Welt
I desire.

15:01.442 --> 15:04.112
Do not lose hope, Ichigo.

15:04.821 --> 15:07.657
There is nothing more painful
for a parent

15:07.865 --> 15:11.577
than killing a child
who is in throes of despair.

15:14.997 --> 15:16.541
So you can still move?

15:17.375 --> 15:18.334
I'm...

15:20.378 --> 15:22.505
a lot like Kurosaki and the others,
you say?

15:23.172 --> 15:24.966
Everything I have done so far...

15:25.299 --> 15:27.176
I've done calmly...

15:27.552 --> 15:31.639
made decisions based on
your so-called balance.

15:32.849 --> 15:36.853
But Kurosaki is an idiot,
so he can't do that...

15:37.770 --> 15:40.648
If he wants to help someone,
he'll just go and help.

15:42.233 --> 15:44.861
Regardless of which way
the balance tilts,

15:45.403 --> 15:47.697
that guy isn't even looking at it.

15:49.157 --> 15:50.658
Inoue's also an idiot.

15:51.075 --> 15:52.410
Sado's also an idiot.

15:52.869 --> 15:54.245
Kuchiki's also an idiot.

15:54.662 --> 15:56.080
And Abarai's also an idiot.

15:58.416 --> 16:03.212
If I appear to be the same
as those idiots...

16:04.213 --> 16:05.590
...that makes me happy.

16:06.883 --> 16:07.758
Is that so?

16:08.217 --> 16:11.470
You are afraid of both
hope and despair, aren't you?

16:13.472 --> 16:15.266
You call it The Almighty,

16:15.600 --> 16:17.810
but it seems you can't
see deep into people's hearts.

16:21.731 --> 16:23.357
What about despair?

16:24.108 --> 16:25.693
I know all about it.

16:32.617 --> 16:33.993
I've overcome it...

16:34.952 --> 16:37.038
time and time again!

16:39.040 --> 16:40.333
It is for this moment,

16:40.625 --> 16:45.254
that I needed you, my son!

16:47.506 --> 16:49.467
"Happy," you say?

16:50.426 --> 16:53.930
I wasn't calling into question
how you felt.

16:54.555 --> 16:57.975
I can't imagine how being with them
benefits you in any way.

16:58.476 --> 16:59.852
That's what I'm saying.

17:00.937 --> 17:03.940
Have you grown by
being with them?

17:04.774 --> 17:06.817
Compared to the few years
you've spent with them...

17:06.984 --> 17:08.527
you should've grown much more

17:08.569 --> 17:12.073
in the instant His Majesty
gave you power.

17:12.990 --> 17:15.117
If friends are there to heighten
one another...

17:15.743 --> 17:19.497
It is not them, but His Majesty
you should risk your life for.

17:20.414 --> 17:23.334
You said the balance is a choice.

17:24.377 --> 17:28.506
I chose to be with them.

17:29.298 --> 17:31.175
There is no self-interest there.

17:31.926 --> 17:33.761
No right, no wrong...

17:34.762 --> 17:37.515
Because we're friends.

17:40.810 --> 17:43.062
I see.
I understand now.

17:43.771 --> 17:46.440
So, you have no intention
of forsaking anything...

17:46.691 --> 17:49.193
even though you were accepted
by His Majesty.

17:50.111 --> 17:53.573
Then at least forsake your life,
Uryu Ishida!

18:01.581 --> 18:02.957
Bankai!

18:04.041 --> 18:07.086
Tensa Zangetsu!

18:15.303 --> 18:18.222
Don't look so grim, Ichigo.

18:18.889 --> 18:22.476
I paid respect to your power.

18:23.227 --> 18:25.354
A new Tensa Zangetsu...

18:25.896 --> 18:30.484
I concluded that
it's a formidable Bankai,

18:31.068 --> 18:33.279
so I broke it in the future.

18:58.554 --> 18:59.847
Bankai!

19:00.931 --> 19:02.350
Bankai, huh?

19:03.476 --> 19:06.062
I like that word.

19:07.063 --> 19:07.938
Ren—!

19:11.317 --> 19:14.862
It's because it's a powerful word
that allows you Soul Reapers

19:14.904 --> 19:19.116
to rise up no matter
what the circumstances.

19:22.953 --> 19:24.664
Thanks to that word,

19:24.789 --> 19:27.917
I was able to crush the hearts
of the Soul Reapers that rose up,

19:27.958 --> 19:30.544
many times over.

19:31.962 --> 19:35.257
You've overcome despair
countless times,

19:35.424 --> 19:37.635
and changed the future, right?

19:38.302 --> 19:40.888
Do you understand
why you were able to do that?

19:41.639 --> 19:44.392
It was because I wasn't there.

19:45.393 --> 19:46.727
My dear Ichigo...

19:46.936 --> 19:48.813
Try and change the future.
Show me.

19:49.271 --> 19:52.608
No matter how magnificent
that future may be...

19:53.234 --> 19:55.695
I will be watching it.

19:59.365 --> 20:05.996
And... I shall cut apart the future
you've changed.

20:07.581 --> 20:11.293
Now, do not despair,

20:11.794 --> 20:13.337
Ichigo...

20:22.763 --> 20:24.055
<i>Retracing memories</i>

20:24.056 --> 20:27.685
<i>An unexpected gaze</i>

20:27.768 --> 20:30.229
<i>The world I didn't want</i>

20:30.271 --> 20:32.188
<i>I've started breaking it down</i>

20:32.189 --> 20:34.859
<i>Lean on each other and face forward</i>

20:34.900 --> 20:37.528
<i>I want to change my fate</i>

20:37.611 --> 20:40.740
<i>All the voices shout</i>

20:40.781 --> 20:42.908
<i>The sound rang out</i>

20:58.340 --> 21:00.884
<i>I saw countless scattered shadows</i>

21:00.885 --> 21:03.220
<i>and I laughed</i>

21:03.387 --> 21:05.639
<i>A world that's lost its color</i>

21:05.681 --> 21:07.975
<i>I'll illuminate it again</i>

21:08.058 --> 21:10.644
<i>Broken and lamenting</i>

21:10.728 --> 21:13.272
<i>The end of the dream</i>

21:13.355 --> 21:17.859
<i>Shaking free from it over and over again
with a still-connected heart</i>

21:17.860 --> 21:23.531
<i>I'll protect today,
the path I've walked all this time</i>

21:23.532 --> 21:24.575
<i>Break it</i>

21:24.700 --> 21:27.161
<i>Tear the future apart, call my name</i>

21:27.203 --> 21:30.205
<i>Turn your back on your predetermined past</i>

21:30.206 --> 21:33.082
<i>Today keeps playing with fate</i>

21:33.083 --> 21:35.044
<i>Reclaim it here and now</i>

21:35.127 --> 21:37.754
<i>To the ends of the earth, an unseen dream</i>

21:37.755 --> 21:40.466
<i>With eyes that know the strength
that lies in words</i>

21:40.549 --> 21:43.593
<i>Notice the distorted spiral</i>

21:43.594 --> 21:47.139
<i>My fate has been set in motion</i>

21:47.181 --> 21:51.227
BLEACH: THOUSAND-YEAR BLOOD WAR

21:54.522 --> 21:56.482
Why are you
looking at me like that?

21:57.733 --> 21:59.443
Did you think I was disappointed

22:00.277 --> 22:03.447
that His Majesty robbed me
of my power?

22:05.157 --> 22:06.158
Quite the opposite.

22:06.742 --> 22:12.289
I'm actually honored
he didn't take your power...

22:13.332 --> 22:18.379
I'm honored that
he chose to take my power.

22:19.630 --> 22:20.881
Because that means

22:21.507 --> 22:23.467
I'm the only one
who can be of service to him.

22:28.722 --> 22:29.723
Is that so?

22:30.140 --> 22:32.142
Wait, Uryu Ishida.

22:33.477 --> 22:37.147
Transfer your wounds onto me
before you go.

22:39.066 --> 22:41.652
I will... die soon.

22:42.820 --> 22:44.655
Wounded or not...

22:45.865 --> 22:47.324
...that won't change.

22:47.825 --> 22:50.202
What are you saying?!

22:50.953 --> 22:51.996
What's the matter?

22:52.580 --> 22:53.622
Is that pity?

22:54.707 --> 22:59.044
Weren't you trying to kill me
just a moment ago?

22:59.628 --> 23:00.504
But—!

23:01.088 --> 23:02.423
Why are you hesitating?

23:03.507 --> 23:06.218
I thought I told you
to put everything on a balance.

23:07.136 --> 23:09.513
Decisions made without
weighing them on a balance,

23:09.638 --> 23:11.515
made hastily in doubt...

23:12.141 --> 23:14.101
will all end up as regret.

23:15.477 --> 23:20.232
Then weigh that on a balance
as well, Uryu Ishida.

23:21.483 --> 23:25.154
You should go help your friends...

23:42.463 --> 23:44.465
<i>Even if the results won't change...</i>

23:45.215 --> 23:46.884
<i>The point is to decide
as you please.</i>

23:47.509 --> 23:49.970
<i>To move forward as you please.</i>

23:53.307 --> 23:54.475
<i>I have no regrets.</i>

23:56.518 --> 23:57.603
<i>Not one...</i>

24:07.363 --> 24:09.323
<i>We are drawn to each other</i>

24:10.324 --> 24:11.533
<i>Like drops of water</i>

24:11.951 --> 24:13.035
<i>Like the planets</i>

24:14.453 --> 24:16.580
<i>We repulse each other</i>

24:17.665 --> 24:18.707
<i>Like magnets</i>

24:19.291 --> 24:20.584
<i>Like the colors of our skin...</i>
